+## After the agents return (coordinator)
+
+1. Read each report. Discard any `fixed` claim whose `check` run doesn't show exit 0 after the last edit.
+2. **Conflicts:** compare `files_changed` across the three reports. Two agents should never touch the same file. If they did, reconcile by hand. Also compare `decisions`. If two agents decided opposite things about the same scope, settle that before merging.
+3. Merge the worktrees one at a time and run the **full suite** after each merge.
+4. Spot-check each diff for masking: skipped tests, loosened assertions, longer timeouts, or catch-and-ignore.
+5. Pick up any `blocked` item myself, because it means a change to shared code that the parallel agents weren't allowed to make.
